0..77 Comment "// A thunk crosses by its image: what it captures, and the declarations homed"
78..140 Comment "// at its world that it names. No former marks a mobile thunk."
141..143 Comment "//"
144..219 Comment "// A thunk is code over an environment, and the environment is what crosses"
220..293 Comment "// with it. Its image is read where it is formed, so a thunk crosses when"
294..356 Comment "// every capture and every homed declaration it names crosses."
357..359 Comment "//"
360..437 Comment "// Each declaration forms a thunk at the seat and returns it to the operator."
438..514 Comment "// The thunks are closed, or over an integer, a marked report or a handle to"
515..592 Comment "// an integer. The image\'s three axes are the capture rules, so every capture"
593..652 Comment "// stands at no region, at ω and at the thunk\'s own world."
653..655 Comment "//"
656..737 Comment "// - see: `pathological/worlds/closure-axes.gandr` — what a thunk captures that"
738..748 Comment "//   stays"
749..823 Comment "// - see: Epstein, Black and Peyton Jones, \"Towards Haskell in the Cloud\","
824..895 Comment "//   Haskell 2011 — a closure crosses as its code and its environment"
897..971 Comment "// The operator\'s and the seat\'s worlds, and the seat\'s sealed side of the"
972..1016 Comment "// exchange, its report alone marked mobile."
